Clean Django Flow (Easy to Understand)
    First: Core Idea
    Project = Entire website (configuration + entry point)
    App = A module/feature (like blogs, users, orders)

    Example:
        Project = MYBlogs
        Apps = blogs, users, payments

Step-by-Step Setup
1. Install & Create Virtual Environment
    python -m venv django_tutorial

    Activate:
    Linux/Mac:
    source django_tutorial/bin/activate

    Windows:
    django_tutorial\Scripts\activate

2. Install Django
    pip install django (before running this command you should be in venv)

3. Create Project (Main Container)
    django-admin startproject MYBlogs

    Folder structure:
    MYBlogs/
    ├── manage.py   ⭐ (main entry point)
    └── MYBlogs/
        ├── settings.py   ⚙️ config
        ├── urls.py       🌐 main routing
        ├── asgi.py
        └── wsgi.py

4. Run Server
    python manage.py runserver

5. Initial DB Setup
    python manage.py makemigrations
    python manage.py migrate

Now Real Development Starts (Apps)
6. Create App
    python manage.py startapp blogs

    Folder structure:
    blogs/
    ├── views.py      ⭐ logic
    ├── models.py     🗄️ database
    ├── tests.py
    ├── admin.py
    └── apps.py

7. Register App (VERY IMPORTANT)
    In settings.py
    INSTALLED_APPS = [
        'blogs',
    ]

8. URL Wiring (Project ↔ App)

    Step A: Create blogs/urls.py (Manually create this file if it is not present under the blogs app)
    Create blogs/urls.py
    from django.urls import path
    from yarl import URL
    from . import views

    urlpatterns = [
        path('', views.home),
    ]

    Step B: Connect App URLs to Project
    👉 In MYBlogs/urls.py
    from django.urls import path, include

    urlpatterns = [
        path('blogs/', include('blogs.urls')),
    ]

9. Write Logic (Views)
    In blogs/views.py
    from django.http import HttpResponse

    def home(request):
        return HttpResponse("Hello, this is Blogs App")

    So this home function will called by blogs, then blogs will internally connected to MYBlogs.

10. Final Flow (VERY IMPORTANT)
    User hits URL → Project urls.py → App urls.py → View → Response

    localhost:8000/blogs/
            ↓
    MYBlogs/urls.py
            ↓
    blogs/urls.py
            ↓
    views.py (home function)
            ↓
    Response shown

| Feature     | Project (MYBlogs)   | App (blogs)          |
| ----------- | ------------------- | -------------------- |
| Purpose     | Whole website       | Specific feature     |
| Contains    | settings, main urls | models, views, logic |
| Entry point | manage.py           | No                   |
| Reusability | ❌                   | ✅ reusable           |
